regfile eHISI_USB_DEVICE {
    name = "HiSilicon USB 2.0 device controller (DesignWare DWC_otg, device mode)";
    desc = "
    HiSilicon USB 2.0 device controller at 0x10080000: a Synopsys DesignWare Cores USB 2.0 Hi-Speed On-The-Go (DWC_otg, \"dwc2\" register map, scatter/gather DMA and dedicated TX FIFO configuration, ADP/LPM/HNP/SRP, UTMI+ 16-bit PHY interface) used in device mode, with up to 16 IN and 16 OUT endpoints. The same core is documented in the data sheet with its host registers, but the host EHCI/OHCI pair at 0x100B0000 / 0x100A0000 is a separate controller (`eHISI_USB_EHCI` / `eHISI_USB_OHCI`); both share one UTMI PHY and are switched by MISC_CTRL30[usb_chipid] (0 = host, 1 = device; with usb2_phy_dmpulldown / usb2_phy_dppulldown 1 for host and 0 for device) and reset/clocked through PERI_CRG46 (DS 12.7.3). Interrupt: VIC interrupt 10 (USB_DEV).
    Layout: global registers 0x000..0x060 (GOTGCTL .. GADPCTL), FIFO size registers (HPTXFSIZ 0x100, DIEPTXF[15] at 0x104 + 4 x (n - 1), the data sheet's DPTXFSIZN / DIEPTXFN, shared-FIFO and dedicated-FIFO views of the same registers), device registers DCFG .. DEACHINTMSK 0x800..0x83C, per-endpoint interrupt mask registers DIEPEACHMSKN[16] (0x840) / DOEPEACHMSKN[16] (0x880) and per-endpoint register sets: IN_EP0 @ 0x900, IN_EP[1..15] @ 0x920 + 0x20 x (n - 1), OUT_EP0 @ 0xB00, OUT_EP[1..15] @ 0xB20 + 0x20 x (n - 1) (control, interrupt, transfer size, DMA address and DMA buffer address, plus the TX FIFO status DTXFSTS for IN endpoints). The data sheet's register tables use name suffixes N/n for the endpoint index.
    Registers are from the Hi3518E V20X/Hi3516C V200 data sheet issue 02 (2017-06-12), section 12.7.5.2 (`datasheet` text lines 86100-90660); descriptions use the data sheet text; scrambled tables are rebuilt (see the register descriptions of GRSTCTL, DIEPINT, DOEPINT). The data sheet also lists DTKNQR3 / DTKNQR4 at the addresses of DTHRCTL / DIEPEMPMSK; they are not modelled separately. Host-mode registers of the core (HCFG, HFIR, HPRT, HC channel registers, PCGCCTL) and the FIFO data windows are not described in the data sheet (host mode runs through the EHCI/OHCI pair) and are not modelled. Not hardware verified.
";

    reg {
        name = "Micro-frame length configuration register";
        desc = "INTNREG00 is a micro-frame length configuration register.

Data sheet 12.7.5.2 INTNREG00 (offset 0x90, printed page 12-161, `Hi3518EV20X-Hi3516CV200-Datasheet.txt` line 86107).";

        field {
            name = "val";
            desc = "Value of the micro-frame counter. This register is used only for emulation. In normal mode, the micro-frame length is 125 us defined by the protocol. During emulation, you can change the micro-frame length by configuring this register as required to";
            sw = rw;
            hw = r;
            reset = 0x0;
        } val[13:1];

        enum INTNREG00_en_enum {
            DISABLED = 0 { name = "Disabled"; desc = "disabled"; };
            ENABLED = 1 { name = "Enabled"; desc = "enabled"; };
        };

        field {
            name = "en";
            desc = "reduce the emulation time. Micro-frame length register enable";
            sw = rw;
            hw = r;
            encode = INTNREG00_en_enum;
            reset = 0x0;
        } en[0:0];
    } INTNREG00 @ 0x90;

    reg {
        name = "PBUF OUT/IN register";
        desc = "INSNREG01 is a PBUF out/in configuration register.

